    },
    "message": "Build the views of the phases from the rows, and give the update kernels their fields from them\n\nrules/world_view.rs makes what WorldView.from_world and after_state_update provide as a snapshot of\nplain Rust values, with the same audit hash. The phases' steps return a WorldView whose Python parts\nare made when a Python reader first asks. The psychology and social kernels read the zone's\nconditions, the body record, the group (with the household override), information pressure and\nrequired sleep from it instead of AgentView.__dict__, and the information kernel shares the group rule.\n\nAdd the python_rules mark, which turns the Rust dispatch off for a test, with a lint that fails when\na ported name is patched without it. Add a shadow that compares every field of each view bit by bit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
